    "beae-test-blp": {
      "be76480_html": "N/A",
      "be430210269_html": "Tax included. ",
      "be72458158275_html": "<a href=\"{{shop.shipping_policy.url}}\">Shipping</a> calculated at checkout.",
      "be165221068_html": "Creating a beautiful outdoor garden starts with choosing the right plants. Whether you have a spacious backyard or a small balcony, here’s how to select plants that will thrive in your outdoor space:",
      "be1897037342_html": "1. Assess Your Sunlight",
      "be1042508655_html": "Observe how much sunlight your outdoor space receives throughout the day. Plants like succulents and cacti love full sun, while ferns and hostas prefer shade.",
      "be1273043259_html": "2. Consider Your Climate",
      "be1193596370_html": "Choose plants that are well-suited to your local climate. If you live in a dry area, opt for drought-tolerant plants like lavender or yucca.",
      "be2145111408_html": "3. Plan for Growth",
      "be428208866_html": "4. Make sure to consider the mature size of the plants you choose. Some may grow larger than expected and need more space to thrive.",
      "be571706898_html": "4. Mix and Match",
      "be365138619_html": "Combine different textures, colors, and heights to create a visually interesting and dynamic garden. Pair tall plants like Bird of Paradise with ground covers or low-growing succulents.",
      "be573313853_html": "By selecting the right plants, you can create a vibrant and thriving outdoor space that reflects your style and needs.",
      "be1209131241_html": "Previous",
      "be2424595_html": "Next",
