    "beae-dasdasd-dasdasd": {
      "be76480_html": "N/A",
      "be430210269_html": "Tax included. ",
      "be72458158275_html": "<a href=\"{{shop.shipping_policy.url}}\">Shipping</a> calculated at checkout.",
      "be2090838752_html": "Frequently asked questions",
      "be1420819198_html": "Quick Answers",
      "be2004911080_html": "San-o-Agri Extra",
      "be1998906082_html": "San-o-Agri Light",
      "be268489182_html": "San-O-Baby Accessories & Toys",
      "be230257944_html": "San-O-Baby Topical Spray",
      "be2057849421_html": "San-O-Doc",
      "be952749464_html": "San-O-Eczema",
      "be631117319_html": "San-O-Foot",
      "be1910279427_html": "San-O-Fresh",
      "be1378365334_html": "San-O-Intimate",
      "be579850327_html": "San-Ocular",
      "be1922235209_html": "San-O-Sport",
      "be2057864380_html": "San-O-Tat",
      "be1922960359_html": "San-O-Tizer",
      "be2057866426_html": "San-O-Vet",
      "be1954485444_html": "San-O-Vet Eyecare",
      "be1925905128_html": "San-O-Wound",
      "be1180400975_html": "MOON Aftersun",
      "be666600537_html": "San-O-Ocular",
      "be1872211616_html": " What is HOCl and how is SanOT different from alcohol, bleach or quats?",
      "be146526131_html": "Which microbes does it act on?",
      "be1742128982_html": "Where can I use it, how often, and what is “contact time”?",
      "be464484343_html": " Do I need to clean first or rinse after?",
      "be369114068_html": "Is SanOT food-grade and medical-grade?",
      "be753521399_html": "What does it smell like?",
      "be2093562032_html": "Does HOCl lead to antimicrobial resistance?",
      "be1261240045_html": "Can I decant it or use it in foggers, humidifiers or HVAC?",
      "be241535854_html": " What if small amounts contact food or are incidentally ingested?",
      "be1635367347_html": "Which SanOT product should I choose?",
      "be800679950_html": "Are there any disclaimers or precautions when considering SanOT products",
      "be1942287050_html": "Hypochlorous acid (HOCl) is the same antimicrobial your white blood cells produce. SanOT’s water-based formulations reduce microbial load quickly when used as directed—without the flammability/dehydration of alcohols or the harshness often associated with bleach or certain quats. Clean, comfortable finish for frequent use.",
      "be2010811025_html": "Proven effective against a broad scope of bacteria, fungi, spores, and viruses when used as directed (see each product’s intended use).",
      "be1343742131_html": "Use on the areas listed for each product (skin/eyes/food/gear/animals/plants/surfaces). You may apply frequently—even back-to-back. Maintain ~60–90 seconds contact time (keep the area visibly wet) or allow to air-dry, unless the page states otherwise.",
      "be1430268432_html": "If soiled, clean first (water; or appropriate detergent for heavier soiling), then apply. Most uses are no-rinse; for food or mouth-contact items, you may wipe/rinse if you prefer.",
      "be466096780_html": "Yes. All SanOT HOCl is produced to food- and medical-grade standards for antimicrobial efficacy. Where helpful for the audience, some pages also show Halaal and HACCP-suitable badges.",
      "be1877767551_html": "A light, clean sea-water / ozone-like note that dissipates quickly.",
      "be571818532_html": "HOCl acts via multiple oxidative mechanisms (proteins, lipids, DNA/RNA), so resistance development is considered unlikely. Always use as directed.",
      "be903453334_html": "Yes—into clean, compatible containers/devices only. For ULV/fogging/HVAC, follow facility SOPs. Do not heat or mix with additives.",
      "be240657394_html": "Food-grade formulas are intended for directed food uses; they are not beverages. Incidental residue from food applications is expected; for large accidental ingestion, drink water.",
      "be1973010887664_html": "<ul><li><b>Skin/eyes (human):</b> San-Ocular, San-O-Wound, San-O-Eczema, MOON Aftersun, San-O-Sport (skin).\n</li><li><b>Baby:</b> San-O-Baby Topical (skin), San-O-Baby Accessories &amp; Toys (objects).\n</li><li><b>Intimate:</b> San-O-Intimate (external, intravaginal, toy hygiene).\n</li><li><b>Surfaces/air: </b>San-O-Tizer (general), San-O-Doc (clinical).\n</li><li><b>Food:</b> San-O-Fresh.\n</li><li><b>Veterinary/animals:</b> San-O-Vet (general), San-O-Vet Eyecare (ocular).\n</li><li><b>Agri:</b> San-O-Agri Light (home/nursery), San-O-Agri Extra (high-load/agri &amp; packhouse).</li></ul><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div>",
      "be1025157177_html": "Avoid direct eye contact unless the product specifically indicates ocular use; wipe/rinse metals after use (not typically required for 316 stainless steel); avoid sensitive fabrics; if sensitivity occurs, rinse with cool water and discontinue; do not mix with other chemicals/products; if ingested flush with plenty of clean water.",
      "be1840590792_html": "San-O-Agri Extra",
      "be1508067001_html": "Where and how should I use it (vs Light)?",
      "be1982419371_html": "What systems/materials is it suitable for?",
      "be398375912_html": "A higher-strength option for high-load zones (greenhouses, packhouses, wash lines). Dilute to suit foliar sprays, tools/equipment sanitation, post-harvest rinses and room/line turnover per your SOPs.",
      "be703613670_html": "Structures, walkways, tools/trays, harvest totes, wash lines, packaging benches, cold-room seals, transport crates and irrigation/hydro hardware—compatible with sprayers, misters, foggers and wash lines. Does not adversely affect pollinators when used as directed.",
      "be1834585794_html": "San-O-Agri Light",
      "be64430939_html": "What plants/environments and tasks is it for?",
      "be2026868019_html": "Is it a pesticide? Will it affect pollinators?",
      "be1007581162_html": "For homes and nurseries—indoor, greenhouse and garden plants. Use for microbial hygiene on leaves/canopies, benches, trays, tools, propagation/cuttings, seed/seedling prep and plant wound sites.",
      "be924137120_html": "Not a pesticide; it targets microbial hygiene. It may disrupt pest life cycles indirectly by improving surface hygiene, but it’s not intended for insects. Does not adversely affect pollinators when used as directed.",
      "be779503815_html": "San-O-Baby Accessories &amp; Toys",
      "be691229650_html": "Which items/materials and do I need to rinse?",
      "be676668280_html": "Is it safe for everyday nursery use?",
      "be203986039_html": "Can I use it on wood, fabric or electronics?",
      "be1612917366_html": "What’s the difference between this and San-O-Baby Topical Spray?",
      "be1005985571_html": "Use on hard, non-porous baby items: pacifiers, nipples, bottles, utensils, teethers, toys, play mats, changing tables, high chairs, lunch boxes, stroller trays, etc. Mist to wet; allow contact time; air-dry. For mouth-contact items, you may wipe or rinse if preferred.",
      "be1383097656_html": "Yes—food- and medical-grade; targets common nursery/clinic pathogens; leaves no residue when used as directed.",
      "be671941023_html": "Wood: light mist and wipe—don’t saturate. Fabrics: spot-test; avoid soaking. Electronics: spray a cloth and wipe housings (avoid ports).",
      "be2142777448_html": "Accessories &amp; Toys is for objects/surfaces; Topical Spray is for skin.",
      "be110016564_html": "San-O-Baby Topical Spray&nbsp;",
      "be539148422_html": " From what age and for which routines?",
      "be129312174_html": "Can I follow with barrier creams or use soaked gauze?",
      "be923297398_html": "How often can I use it?",
      "be1173408780_html": "From infancy for nappy care, folds, scrapes, bites and minor irritations. Medical-grade antiseptic; anti-inflammatory; won’t strip natural oils.",
      "be1133848933_html": "Yes—apply first, allow contact time, then layer your barrier cream/gel. For comfort, you can briefly apply gauze/tissue soaked with product and discard after use.",
      "be663455923_html": "As often as needed.",
      "be1297256675_html": "What can I disinfect—devices, PPE, rooms?",
      "be65686809_html": "How does it slot into workflows?",
      "be33227300_html": "Use on clinical surfaces, non-critical devices, probes, prosthetics, beds and PPE (masks, gloves, shields) per SOPs; suitable for light room-misting where appropriate.",
      "be141749956_html": "Pre-clean visible soil, then disinfect with ~60–90 s contact time. Supports fast turnover and end-of-day cleaning; follow device IFUs.",
      "be18124860_html": "Can I combine with prescribed treatments or emollients? Will it dry my skin?",
      "be1939100212_html": "How often and any comfort tips?",
      "be301016293_html": "Yes—apply San-O-Eczema first, allow contact time, then layer your prescribed cream/gel or emollient. It’s anti-inflammatory and won’t strip natural oils.",
      "be1334927033_html": "Use multiple times daily. For comfort, briefly apply soaked gauze to the area, then discard.",
      "be861557724_html": "Athlete’s foot and odour—how should I use it and on what?",
      "be214523408_html": "Spray soles, heels, between toes and around nail edges; allow contact time; air-dry. For odour control, lightly mist shoes and socks to address odour-causing bacteria.",
      "be2022433858_html": "As frequently as needed.",
      "be528439649_html": "What foods and settings is it for? Do I need to rinse?",
      "be1636055499_html": "Can it help with shelf life and mould?",
      "be2127430812_html": "Compliance?",
      "be1102095239_html": "Use at home or in restaurants on freshly picked produce, store-bought groceries, meats, poultry and seafood. Also for utensils and prep surfaces. Mist to wet; allow contact time; no rinsing required (rinse optional).",
      "be1549382233_html": "Yes—spray before storing foods to help support shelf life in and out of the fridge. You can also spray over visible mould on treated areas to help prevent spread.",
      "be534330887_html": "Food- and medical-grade; Halaal; suitable for HACCP environments.",
      "be889775032_html": "External, intravaginal and toy use—pH, odour, residue?",
      "be1038963570_html": "What is it tested against? Does it prevent STIs or act as contraception?",
      "be1681348182_html": "Toy material notes",
      "be1844414345_html": "Formulated for topical and intravaginal care and hygienic toy surfaces. pH-considerate, neutralises odour-causing bacteria, dries without residue.",
      "be1192479240_html": "Lab-tested effective against Herpes virus and Candida albicans, among others. It is not a contraceptive and does not prevent STIs.",
      "be799926627_html": "Best on non-porous materials (silicone, ABS, stainless steel). For porous/painted items or electronics, follow manufacturer guidance (spray cloth, not ports).",
      "be1635521718_html": "Can I spray it into my eyes? What about contact lenses?",
      "be998395931_html": "What symptoms can it help with?",
      "be1191057860_html": "Yes—hold ~10 cm away and spray into/onto eyes and lids; blink to distribute. Use before inserting or after removing contact lenses; don’t spray onto lenses while worn.",
      "be243501291_html": "Useful for dryness/irritation and hygiene around pink-eye/stye-related symptoms; suitable for regular daily routines.",
      "be1025604457_html": "What’s it for—skin or equipment?",
      "be1201313511_html": "How do I use it—and can it be a cooling mist?",
      "be1076402309_html": " Will it leave stickiness or odour?",
      "be850880063_html": "Both. Topically for scratches, chafing, rashes, minor scrapes/blisters and post-workout irritation; and for equipment/gear from yoga mats and benches to helmets, gloves, mouth guards, weights, bars and pads.",
      "be1089146400_html": "Skin: spray, maintain contact time, air-dry; may be used as a light cooling mist on intact skin. Gear: spray non-porous surfaces, allow contact time, then wipe or dry.",
      "be305936763_html": "No sticky residues; helps deodorise shoes, pads and bags.",
      "be156294190_html": "When do I use it—pre, during or after?",
      "be354904521_html": "Can I soak jewellery in it?",
      "be2062960275_html": "How often may I apply—and can I layer balms?",
      "be1788804399_html": "Will it fade tattoo ink or alter colours?",
      "be183077035_html": "All three: pre-procedure prep, in-process hygiene and post-procedure aftercare (as advised by your professional).",
      "be1273179706_html": "Do not soak jewellery. You may disinfect and wipe jewellery surfaces (or saturate a sterile swab/gauze) per studio guidance.",
      "be1156704240_html": "You may reapply multiple times in succession before using your prescribed cream/gel; frequent application generally improves comfort and hygiene.",
      "be592037918_html": "No—won’t bleach or lift colour when used as directed.",
      "be731439200_html": "What does it cover—hands, surfaces, air?",
      "be874795420_html": "How is it different from alcohol sanitisers?",
      "be407911744_html": "A versatile disinfectant for hands/skin, high-touch surfaces and air disinfection (misting/fogging) from home to industrial settings (ULV/foggers/HVAC per SOPs).",
      "be322181121_html": "Food- and medical-grade, Halaal, water-based and non-dehydrating while effective against bacteria, fungi and viruses when used as directed.",
      "be1750477978_html": "What is it used for—in clinics, shelters and farms?",
      "be1712820720_html": "How do I apply it in practice?",
      "be1274500799_html": "Think of it as a combo of Tizer + Wound + Doc for animals: everyday skin/coat and wound hygiene, environmental control and equipment sanitation. Suitable pre-, during and post-operations, during gestation, and for dental/oral/ear hygiene support.",
      "be1007184361_html": "Spray or wipe for skin/coat and tools; fog/mist for enclosures as per SOPs. Effective against common animal-shelter and farm-animal pathogens when used as directed.",
      "be1576706496_html": "Can I spray directly into the eye and how often?",
      "be742123204_html": "Which issues can it help with?",
      "be1093566647_html": "Yes—hold ~10 cm away and spray into/onto eyes and lids, or apply with a clean pad. Use multiple times daily or as advised by your vet.",
      "be16158535_html": "Supports ocular hygiene for infections/irritations, allergies and tear-stain residues across species (pets, birds, farm animals, reptiles).",
      "be1241192362_html": "Which wounds/irritations is it for, and how often?",
      "be399744380_html": "Does it help with biofilm?",
      "be317101146_html": "For cuts, abrasions, minor burns, bites/stings, rashes, topical inflammation and post-procedure sites as directed. Frequent application can help accelerate recovery.",
      "be328099352_html": "Yes—used in hygiene protocols that help combat biofilm formation on treated areas.",
      "be1308344620_html": "How should I use it—and can I chill it?",
      "be1665084251_html": "Is it a sunscreen?",
      "be1018790366_html": "Mist generously on sun-exposed skin; allow to dry. You can reapply multiple times in succession. For extra comfort, store in a cooler box or fridge before use.",
      "be174470274_html": "No—MOON Aftersun is not a sunscreen and contains no SPF. Pair with sun protection when outdoors.",
      "be127662261722_html": "<div>Dining room</div>",
      "be828584947_html": "From elegant dining chairs to stylish tables, discover unbeatable deals on everything you need",
      "be282195252_html": "Shop now",
      "be160628911122_html": "<div>Living room</div>",
      "be15690865777_html": "<div>Limited time only—shop now and create your perfect gathering spot!</div>",
      "be19086692518_html": "<div>Bedroom</div>",
      "be359819825106_html": "<div>From modern platform beds to elegant dressers, discover unbeatable deals on everything you need</div>",
      "be1352763075_html": "Scroll to top"
    },
